This is not to denegrate the work done by the mighty and powerful Dev
Team, but....

Remember, Nethack is open source for a reason.  Nethack itself evolved
out of a series of modifications to the game of Hack, and Hack was
originally a recreation of Rogue.  Nethack has spawned its own
competitior in Slash'em, which sees semi-active development.  And there
are plenty of public patches out there, far more now than at any point
before in the game's history: check some of 'em out at
http://bilious.homelinux.org/

Slash'em's existence does not imply that another game cannot arise out
of Nethack's source, indeed I think there's probably a market for a
game that's not quite so *promiscuous* concerning the features it
adopts, but updates more frequently than Nethack.  That's not really
easy to do well, since Nethack's design is very complicated at this
point, but it's an option.

